3. ✅ **SETUP_MICROPYTHON.md updated (hardware fixes)**:
   - Corrected chip type: esp32 (not esp32s3) - CRITICAL for Core2 v1.1
   - Corrected port: /dev/ttyACM0 (not ttyUSB0)
   - Fixed hexadecimal format: 0x0 (not 0)
   - Updated all commands in Linux Quick Start
   - Added troubleshooting section for chip detection

4. ✅ **Firmware backup completed**:
   - Command: `esptool.py --chip esp32 --port /dev/ttyACM0 read_flash 0x0 0x400000 m5stack_core2_backup.bin`
   - Backup saved as: m5stack_core2_backup.bin
   - Size: 4MB (entire flash memory)
   - Time: ~2-3 minutes

5. ✅ **Discovered Core2 firmware distribution model**:
   - Core2 UIFlow firmware is distributed ONLY through M5Burner
   - GitHub releases (github.com/m5stack/uiflow-micropython/releases) contain firmware for Fire, Basic, Atom, etc. but NOT Core2
   - Reason: Core2 has unique hardware (ILI9342C touchscreen, AXP192/AXP2101 power management) requiring specific firmware
   - Manual esptool flashing only works with generic ESP32 firmware (no M5Stack libraries)
   - For Astartes-Gotchi: M5Burner is REQUIRED to get M5Stack libraries

6. ✅ **SETUP_MICROPYTHON.md updated (firmware instructions)**:
